title: Conditional writes
tags: [[Data model]]
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: ?expected_version= makes a single-record write fail with 409 when the metarecord changed since it was read.

The single-record writes — whole-record `PUT`, metarecord `DELETE`, field `POST`,
field `PUT` and `DELETE` by name, the [[refresh|Refreshing a record]] — take an optional `?expected_version=<n>`. When the
metarecord's current version differs, the write is refused with `409`: nothing
written, no revision. It is the optimistic-concurrency primitive sync's propagation
uses, so that a concurrent user write is never overwritten; any client may use it
the same way.

The version being a hash of the content ([[Metarecord version]]), the guard is
''content-based'': a write conditioned on version `H` succeeds even if the metarecord
went from `H` to another state and back in between — the question is "is the state
I read still the state I write against?", and an identical state is that state.
